# s9.grammar -- the om4 language (OMEGESE.md sections 3 and 9, with the gaps of SPEC_GAPS.md as om4 reads
# them) as a grammar over word classes, read left to right. Decision 22: after any prefix exactly one
# rule applies, so a writer's mask always has one parse to extend (tools/omega_ref/omega_next.c checks it).
#
# Notation: `lhs -> alt | alt`; a line starting with `|` continues the rule above. 'w' is the fixed word w.
# Word classes (decided per word from the names in scope, left to right):
#   NUM a number (6.1 spelling, gap G5)  TYPE a type word  OP2 add..ge  OP1 neg not
#   VAR a visible scalar name  ARR a visible local array, array parameter or text  POOL a visible pool
#   (a pool is never an argument, decision 18; a text may be one, gap G6)
#   FNV / FNVOID an earlier function (or the one being written) that returns a value / nothing
#   NEWNAME any other name  STR the quoted bytes of a text line  REST the rest of a note line
#   NL end of line  EOF end of input.  _ is the empty sequence.
# @args stands for the arguments of the function just read: `value` per scalar parameter, `arrarg` per
# array parameter. Words starting with ! are scope actions (they read no word):
#   !fn !param_s !param_a !ret_val !ret_void !fnend: a function and its signature; !pool !text: a pool or a text;
#   !open !close: a block; !bind_s !bind_a !bind_loop: the new name of this line becomes visible.

program  -> NL program
          | fn_def program
          | 'global' NEWNAME TYPE NUM !pool NL program
          | 'text' NEWNAME STR !text NL program
          | 'note' rest NL program
          | EOF
rest     -> REST | _
fn_def   -> 'fn' NEWNAME !fn params 'to' rettype NL !open body 'end' !close !fnend NL
params   -> NEWNAME ptype params | _
ptype    -> TYPE !param_s | 'view' TYPE NUM !param_a | 'edit' TYPE NUM !param_a
rettype  -> TYPE !ret_val | 'void' !ret_void
body     -> stmt body | _
stmt     -> NL
          | 'if' value NL !open body elsep 'end' !close NL
          | 'while' value boundp NL !open body 'end' !close NL
          | 'for' NEWNAME TYPE value !open !bind_loop NL body 'end' !close NL
          | 'ret' retp NL
          | 'put' anyarr value value NL
          | 'exit' value NL
          | 'note' rest NL
          | FNVOID @args NL
          | VAR eqp value NL
          | NEWNAME eqp newval NL
elsep    -> 'else' !close !open NL body | _
boundp   -> 'bound' NUM | _
retp     -> value | _
eqp      -> '=' | _
newval   -> value !bind_s | 'new' TYPE NUM value !bind_a
value    -> NUM | 'true' | 'false' | VAR
          | OP2 value value | OP1 value | TYPE value
          | 'get' anyarr value | 'len' anyarr
          | 'read' value anyarr value value | 'write' value anyarr value value
          | FNV @args
          | '(' value ')'
arrarg   -> ARR | 'view' ARR | 'edit' ARR
anyarr   -> ARR | POOL
